  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Akari Sorghum Milling Capacity Building Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sector: Sorghum .Town/City: Kapuri Village, South Sudan.Summary: The purpose of this grant is to strengthen Akari Development Association as a sustainable farming cooperative and ensure food security and increased income for its members. ADA will purchase sorghum from its members and process it into clean grains and sorghum flour for resale in commercial markets. ADA will purchase mechanized processing equipment, an improvement on the manual tools they use currently, and receive trainings on food handling as well as entrepreneurship, agronomy, good governance, and financial management. Funds will also be used to produce a group policy manual and a five-year business plan to prepare ADA for future expansion.</narrative>
  </description>
